version 0.11
symbol dc-dc-soic8

description 8-pin step-down converter with exposed pad in SOIC-8
tags buck dc-dc regulator
# Placement rules: 4/5 on the left, 1/2/3/8 on the right, 7 on top, 6/9 on bottom.
# Same-side pins follow natural pin-number order: right side bottom to top 1, 2, 3, 8; left side bottom to top 4, 5; bottom side left to right 6, 9.
# Body width is 16 mm to leave clearance for long pin names like VSENSE and for the vertical pin names of GND/PAD below.
# The bottom pins sit half a millimetre right of centre so the vertical name of GND clears VSENSE.
# The side tails are 7 mm long so a net label can sit on a pin: a label is about 5.5 mm wide and is drawn inside the body
# (spec/symbol.md), so the tail must be long enough to carry it between the connection point and the body edge.
# Pin connection points sit on the 0.5 mm placement lattice (ADR-0057) in both coordinates; rows are 2.5 mm apart (ADR-0058).
pin_name_offset 1.25
field Reference at=[12,11] U
field Value at=[12,-11] dc-dc-soic8

pins
  1  [15,-3.5]    180  length=7
  2  [15,-1]      180  length=7
  3  [15,1.5]     180  length=7
  4  [-15,-1]     0    length=7
  5  [-15,1.5]    0    length=7
  6  [-0.5,-7.5]  90
  7  [0,7.5]      270
  8  [15,4]       180  length=7
  9  [2,-7.5]     90

body
  rect  [-8,-5,8,5]  fill=background  width=0.25
